---
import { href, REPO_URL } from '../../lib/site';
---

<section id="contribute">
  <div class="wrap grid two">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Contribute</p>
      <h2>Regulatory knowledge counts as much as code</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        If you know a regime well, you can tell us what a rule gets wrong, or add a jurisdiction
        yourself. That means a detection rule, a risk taxonomy, a Rego pack and tests, with a
        step-by-step guide in CONTRIBUTING.md.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn primary" href={href('docs/contributing/')}>Contributing guide</a>
        <a class="btn" href={`${REPO_URL}/issues?q=is%3Aopen+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22`}>Good first issues</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card ideas">
      <h3>Wanted right now</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Policy packs for California ADMT, China generative AI and India DPDP</li>
        <li>New jurisdictions: Brazil (LGPD), Colorado AI Act, South Korea, UK</li>
        <li>Review of finding wording by compliance practitioners</li>
        <li>Region aliases that users actually type</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .ideas ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .ideas li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
</style>
